<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Shelburne-Glebe-II.jpg" alt="This plein air painting was re-worked in the studio. The landscape was painted with analogous colors set against a pale blue sky." width="450" height="334" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Shelburne Glebe Meadows. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2014.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Unable to go painting on location today due to the rain, I spent the day in the studio. &nbsp;After working on a commissioned work this morning, I decided to revisit the plein air painting that I did last week at Shelburne Glebe in Lincoln, VA.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I made several changes to the original painting with the aim of creating the feeling of a bigger, more open space. After the painting was dry I scumbled in some cloud formations.</p>